    "finalMessage": "The film is built and plays: headless Chrome rendered frames across the 30 seconds with no console messages, and the frames at `?t=0` and `?t=30` came out the same, so the loop joins. I only looked at still frames (plus one autoplay capture at about 5 seconds), so the motion itself has not been watched in real time.\n\n## Files\n\n```\nindex.html              entry point, import map for three@0.170.0\nsrc/main.js             renderer, render loop, ?t= freeze\nsrc/timeline.js         all timings (open, page turns, pop-ups, close)\nsrc/camera.js           camera keyframes and interpolation\nsrc/stage.js            table and lights\nsrc/paper.js            shared paper helpers (card, box, cone, fold-up animation)\nsrc/book.js             covers, page blocks, three turning leaves\nsrc/worlds/castle.js\nsrc/worlds/jungle.js\nsrc/worlds/port.js\nsrc/worlds/mountains.js\n```\n\n## How to view\n\nFrom this folder, start any static server and open the page:\n\n```\npython3 -m http.server 8000\n```\n\n- **Play:** `http://localhost:8000/index.html` starts automatically at full window size and loops.\n- **Freeze a frame:** `http://localhost:8000/index.html?t=12.5` renders that moment and stops.\n\nIt needs network access to load Three.js from jsDelivr.\n\n## Timeline\n\n| Seconds | What happens |\n|---|---|\n| 0\u20133 | closed book, cover opens |\n| 3\u20138.4 | castle |\n| 9.6\u201314.8 | jungle |\n| 16\u201321.2 | port with boats |\n| 22.4\u201327.6 | snowy peaks |\n| 27.7\u201330 | book closes |\n\nEach world folds flat before the page turns and the next one folds up after.\n\n## Known rough spots\n\n- **Castle path:** the cream path from the gate to the front edge does not show in the frames.\n- **Table planks:** the lines are dense and may shimmer in the distance.\n- **Jungle back wall:** the canopy card shows a couple of stray diagonal lines.\n\nThe workers wrote every file; I planned, reviewed the frames and sent back one round of fixes (page flicker, cloud placement, lighting, camera angle on page turns)."
